{
  "Content that scrolls in a box of its own: the bars shown as told, a pull from the top that asks for what is new, a reach near the end that asks for more. Moved programmatically to a position or to an element.": "",
  "A box that scrolls": "",
  "The JSX children are the content. `showScrollbar` says when the bars show; `scrollTo` and `scrollToElement` move the content programmatically, `onScrolled` tells where it stands.": "",
  "Pull to refresh": "",
  "With `pullToRefresh`, the content pulled down from its top asks `onPullDown`. Set `promise` (or call `release()`) and the panel goes when the work is done.": "",
  "Load more near the end": "",
  "With `loadOnReachBottom`, a scroll within `reachBottomOffset` of the end asks `onReachBottom` once; `release()` lets the next reach ask again, `release(true)` says there is no more. Content that does not fill the box asks at once.": "",
  "The box scrolls with the wheel, the keys when focused, a finger, and programmatically. `direction` locks the other axis; the page behind does not scroll on when the content ends.": "",
  "The design system’s bars. With `onScroll` the thumb shows while the content moves and goes a moment after; with `onHover` while the pointer is over the view or focus is in it; `always` leaves them; `never` hides them, the content still scrolls.": "",
  "From the top, with a finger or the pointer: the content comes down (harder the farther it goes) and the panel above it says to pull, then to release. Let go far enough it refreshes: the spinner turns until `release()` or the promise. A short pull goes back.": "",
  "Within `reachBottomOffset` of the end, `onReachBottom` is asked once; the panel under the content shows meanwhile. Released, the next reach asks again, until `release(true)`. Content that does not fill the box asks at once, and again as it grows.": "",
  "The kit’s, in the kit language, unless the text props say otherwise.": "",
  "A focusable box named by `label`; the arrow keys, Page Up/Down, Home and End scroll it as the browser does.": "",
  "Live regions: “Refreshing…” and “Loading…” are read when they appear.": "",
  "Decorative; the texts say what is going on.": "",
  "A finger that pulls does not scroll the page; a finger that scrolls does not pull.": "",
  "The box. `data-direction`, `data-bars`, `data-scrolling` while the content moves, `data-pull` when pulling is on, `data-pulling` during a pull, `data-pull-state` (`pull`, `release`, `refreshing`), `data-loading`.": "",
  "What holds the children; it moves down during a pull.": "",
  "The panel above the content, its text and the kit’s spinner.": "",
  "The panel under the content while more loads.": "",
  "Unit: the box (`focus`).": "",
  "Units: the two panels (the pull one `release` and `refreshing`) and their texts.": "",
  "The panels’ height; the space between a panel’s spinner and its text.": "",
  "`vertical`, `horizontal` or `both`: which way the content scrolls.": "",
  "When the bars show: `onScroll` while scrolling, `onHover` while the pointer is over the view, `always`, `never`.": "",
  "Pulling the content down from its top asks `onPullDown` for what is new.": "",
  "Scrolling near the end asks `onReachBottom` for more; so does content that does not reach the end.": "",
  "Pixels before the end at which `onReachBottom` is asked.": "",
  "the kit’s texts": "",
  "The pull panel’s texts: while pulling, once far enough, while refreshing.": "",
  "The text under the content while more loads.": "",
  "What screen readers call the scrolling region.": "",
  "The content was pulled down and let go. Load what is new, then `release()`, or set `promise` and the panel goes when it settles.": "",
  "The content was scrolled near its end. Load more, then `release()`; `release(true)` says there is no more and the view stops asking. A `promise` releases too.": "",
  "The position changed: `top`, `left`.": "",
  "To a top, or `{ top, left }`; `smooth` animates.": "",
  "By a distance.": "",
  "Brings an element (or a component) of the content into view.": "",
  "Starts a refresh as a pull would; ends it.": "",
  "Asks for more now; looks at the position again after the content changed.": "",
  "Where the content stands.": "",
  "A refresh or a loading is going on.": "",
